 "report": "cr_mature (matured-label residual feedback, class 3): KILL.\nStep 1 (TRAIN class 3). Exit levels X0 = ask_k + t0 and X1 = bid_k - t1 are always quote levels that occur later on the decoded path. A long winner's X0 is a future bid that is never exceeded before it is first touched (0 of 7.6k runs), so exits happen at running extremes at a stopping time, not at a fixed horizon. Law-free lower bound on the determination lag, j_lb = first event touching both label levels (800 seqs, 2.0M runs, |y|-weighted): median 3, p90 7, p95 11, p99 29 events (outside runs: p99 47). Weight not computable at lag N: 8.1% (N=8), 3.9% (12), 1.3% (24), 0.9% (32). Conservative L >= 32. Exact path-prefix mode table (2400 seqs, component-disjoint fit/held-out): held-out |y|-weighted exact among covered runs is 0.85 / 0.90 / 0.95 / 0.93 at j = 8 / 10 / 16 / 32, with coverage 0.98 / 0.93 / 0.61 / 0.21. Best exact over all runs is 0.84 at j=8-10. The summary key (running ask/bid max/min) peaks at 0.83 at j=10. The label is not a function of the event path up to 32 events (about 5% weighted residual ambiguity), so there is no exact reconstruction.\nStep 2 (VALID, 4 clean folds, p = mean of ft_since_s3/s4; beta, alpha, kappa cross-fitted; held-fold pooled delta Global WP, mean of 4 folds). True labels at L = 2 / 4 / 8 / 12 / 16 / 24 / 32 / 48: +0.0621 / +0.0137 / +0.0008 / +0.0001 / +0.0000 / -0.0002 / -0.0001 / -0.0003. At the conservative L=32 the bootstrap gives -0.00004, CI [-0.0004, +0.0003]. The L=8 result (+0.0008, CI [+0.00003, +0.0017], class 3 +0.0031) reproduces the scout's F3b and is mostly leak. Reconstructed labels (deployable, TRAIN tables with backoff), same L grid: -0.0002 / -0.0000 / -0.0001 / -0.0000 / -0.0001 / -0.0002 / -0.0003 / -0.0004. With L also cross-fitted: -0.00023 pooled, CI [-0.0006, +0.0001]; class 3 -0.0008.\nStep 3 (leak control). The label is swapped with the true label of a run in another sequence that has the identical decoded path up to E_{k+L}, so only the post-E_{k+L} future changes. true_R -> shuf_R: L=2 +0.0619 -> -0.0002; L=4 +0.0136 -> -0.0000; L=8 +0.0011 -> -0.0001; L=12 +0.0007 -> +0.0001; L=16 +0.0005 -> -0.0001. Partner coverage is 0.99 / 0.97 / 0.87 of label weight at L = 8 / 12 / 32. All of the true-label gain disappears when the future is swapped, so it is future information and not path information that the model fails to use.\nVerdict: the deployable signal is <= 0 at every lag (kill threshold +0.0005), and the gain disappears under the legal L. Do not build the per-row algorithm. Side facts that may be useful elsewhere: interior F is touched by both quotes within 2 events (99.7% of interior weight); winners exit at the running extreme of the exit-side quote at a stopping time (p95 11 events). A first-passage or trailing-extreme target representation (scout M2b) is the only lead this leaves open.\nFiles: scripts/cr_mature_{common,lag,hit,feedback}.py; research/campaign_2026-10-01/creative/cr_mature/{hit_lag_report,lag_report,feedback_report}.json, lag_tables_{kp,ks}.npz.",
